  "id": "Compound::DB00473 - Gene::6323",
  "verbalization": "Hexylcaine appears to interact with multiple sodium channel subunits, specifically Scn2a and Scn3a, through binding interactions. These subunits are involved in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, which is critical for neuronal excitation. The observed relationship between Hexylcaine and Scn1a is mediated through the involvement of these subunits in sodium channel function. The evidence suggests that Hexylcaine may modulate sodium channel activity by binding to Scn2a or Scn3a, thereby influencing the activity of Scn1a. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Hexylcaine could exert its effects on neuronal function, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
